    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe new logic lands in sensible units \u2014 `OwnerSoundex` as a centralized single-source-of-truth class mirrors the existing `OwnerHousehold`/`OwnerTelephone`/`OwnerEmail` idiom nicely, and routing all three callers (`CheckOwnerIdentityUnique`, `AssignPossibleDuplicate`, the mapper) through `OwnerIdentity.of`/`key` keeps derivation consolidated. `OwnerHousehold` correctly survives because `householdId` is still needed by `AssignHousehold`/`AssignHouseholdSize`/`CapMembershipLevel`. But two structural issues:\n\n**1. Duplicated SHA-256\u2192hex boilerplate.** `OwnerIdentity.sha256hex` (new) and `OwnerHousehold.idFor` now contain the same hand-rolled `MessageDigest.getInstance(\"SHA-256\")` \u2192 byte loop \u2192 `String.format(\"%02x\")` \u2192 `NoSuchAlgorithmException`-wrapped-as-`IllegalStateException` sequence. The outputs differ (lower vs upper case, full vs 12-char truncation) but the digest-and-hex-encode mechanism is identical across two classes in the same package. A maintainer would expect one shared helper (e.g. a small `Sha256`/hashing util both call, with case/length as parameters) rather than two copies that can drift. The diff introduced the second copy; this is the moment to extract it.\n\n**2. Stale javadoc left inconsistent with the change \u2014 including a self-contradiction inside an edited file.** The identity key no longer folds in `householdId`, but three doc comments still describe it that way:\n- `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique.java:11` \u2014 \"identityKey (normalised telephone, email and household together)\". The author rewrote the second paragraph of *this same class's* javadoc (line 21-22) to say \"last name's Soundex\", so the class now contradicts itself in adjacent paragraphs.\n- `DuplicateIdentityException.java:6` \u2014 \"the request matches on normalised telephone, email and household together\".\n- `DuplicateIdentityExceptionHandler.java:11-12` \u2014 \"whole identityKey (normalised telephone, email and household together)\".\n\nThese weren't touched by the diff but are now wrong as a direct consequence of it; update them to reference the telephone/email/last-name-Soundex composition so the doc set stays coherent with `OwnerIdentity`.",
